  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hear me out what if we replaced the camera with a phone that you can use to chat with people and send and take pictures. Maybe add a social vrchat app to post pictures in-game(a bit too much but fun). VRC+ Phone backgrounds and cases like the menu background (adds more reasoning to have vrc+). I feel like vrchat could use a chat tool to chat/send pics to people in other worlds like seen in games like recroom. Having a phone like system adds like a little bit of flair to the game and spices it up a bit. Also having a chat system to chat with friends just helps if you don't have said friends discord or are not comfortable with sharing. It's just a little bit more fun and a cool feature that could improve how people communicate in vrc. Sometimes taking off headset to just type in discord is too much and some peoples pc just cant run vr and discord at the same time, that could possibly help some people as well. It might seem like a useless feature but I honestly think it could change vrc for good.",
